<!--
  1vivy personal crDroid 16.0 ROM - OnePlus SM8850 (infiniti, macan, macanc,
  fairlady).

  Drop into .repo/local_manifests/ after:

      repo init -u https://github.com/crdroidandroid/android.git -b 16.0
      # base manifest pinned at a311bc97e4784ee24e8f97e377d06bdbff85b4bb

  then `repo sync`.

  THIS MANIFEST IS THE OUTSIDE-DEVELOPER COMPOSITION, NOT THE PROMOTED GRAPH.

  infiniti-camera-port/local_manifest pins the eight camera-port source repos
  at their PROMOTED heads, which already contain the eight patch series. A
  consumer of that manifest must never run patches/patch/ on top - it would
  double-apply. This manifest deliberately takes the other route: the eight
  source targets are pinned at the profile's BASE commits, and the published
  profile transforms them into the promoted trees.

  After sync, follow the "Downstream porter quick start" in the patches
  repository README: run apply-patches.py in check mode against profile
  infiniti-crdroid-16.0, then "repo start infiniti-crdroid-16.0" over the eight
  targets listed there, then run it again in apply mode.

  Applying the profile is therefore MANDATORY here, and forbidden for consumers
  of the promoted manifest. Each revision below that is a bare 40-char SHA is a
  series base_sha copied from patches/patch/series.json; once the profile is
  applied each of those targets reaches the corresponding head_sha, which
  equals the promoted contract head.

  The five device trees are 1vivy forks. Their 16.0 lanes were cut at the
  immutable pre-lane pin table, and for the two that are also profile targets
  the lane tip IS the profile base:

      device/oneplus/infiniti        16.0 = ba57c74670f9... = series base_sha
      device/oneplus/sm8850-common   16.0 = 0522cdc6164b... = series base_sha

  The six sync-only prerequisites are consumed verbatim from
  infiniti-camera-port; they are pure sync inputs and are never patch targets.

  Only lineage_infiniti-bp4a-userdebug is built and runtime-validated upstream.
  macan, macanc and fairlady are present for source closure and static lunch
  resolution; no runtime result is implied for them.
-->
